    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in Sjögren:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " dry mouth: cevimeline 30 mg PO TID (or pilocarpine 5 mg) can stim saliva; ⍉w bronchospasm or closed-angle glaucoma."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) dose, dry mouth in Sjögren's syndrome:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 30 mg taken three times a day; insuff safety info to support doses > 30 mg tid."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " uncontrolled asthma, known hypersensitivity to cevimeline, and when miosis = undesirable, ex, acute iritis and narrow-angle (angle-closure) glaucoma."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) cardiovasc:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Can potentially alt ♡ conduction and/or HR; pts w sig cardiovasc dz may be unable to compensate for transient chgs in hemodynamics or rhythm; use w caution and under close medical supervision in pts w Hx of cardiovasc dz evidenced by angina pectoris or MI."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) pulm:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Can potentially ↑ airway resistance, bronchial smooth musc tone, and bronchial secretions; administer w caution and w close medical supervision to pts w controlled asthma, chronic bronchitis, or COPD."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) ocular:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Ophthalmic formulations of muscarinic agonists reported to cause visual blurring which may result in ↓ visual acuity, esp @ night and in pts w central lens chgs, and to cause impairment of depth perception; caution advised while driving @ night or performing hazardous activities in ↓lighting."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) CYP2D6/CYP3A3/4 interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Drugs which inhibit CYP2D6 and CYP3A3/4 also inhibit the met of cevimeline; use w caution in pts known or sus to be deficient in CYP2D6 activity, as they may be @ ↑ risk of adverse events. Use w caution in pts taking β adrenergic antagonists, ←the possibility of conduction disturb."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) OD signs:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Toxicity = exaggerated parasympathomimetic effects: HA, visual disturb, lacrimation, sweating, resp distress, GI spasm, N/V/D, AV block, tachy, brady, hypotension, HTN, shock, mental confusion, ♡ arrhythmia, and tremors."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cevimeline (Evoxac) OD mgnt:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Mgnt as for other muscarinic agonists w gen supportive measures; if medically indicated, atropine may be of value as an antidote for emergency use in pts who have had an OD; Epi may also be of value in severe cardiovasc depression or bronchoconstrict."
     }
    ]
   }
